From: tabS3 bring-up <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] iio: smgr_light: the firmware reports whole lux

The ambient light samples of the Sensor Manager's PROX_LIGHT sensor hold
the illuminance in whole lux, not Q16: on the SM-T825's CM3323 the first
value reads 64 in a room, drops to 0 under a thumb and comes back, while
the Q16 reading was a constant 0.001 lux. The second value is a raw
count (about 3100, rising to 4500 in the dark) and is not exposed.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5-1
---
diff -ruN a/drivers/iio/light/smgr_light.c b/drivers/iio/light/smgr_light.c
--- a/drivers/iio/light/smgr_light.c	2026-10-14 10:21:27.760098381 +0300
+++ b/drivers/iio/light/smgr_light.c	2026-10-14 10:21:27.781494839 +0300
@@ -5,10 +5,11 @@
  * Derived from the Sensor Manager accelerometer driver,
  * Copyright (c) 2022, Yassine Oudjana <y.oudjana@protonmail.com>
  *
- * The Sensor Manager's PROX_LIGHT sensor reports illuminance as Q16 lux.
- * This driver covers sensor cores whose first data type is the ambient
- * light sensor (for example a Capella CM3323 with no proximity sensor);
- * a proximity data type is not handled yet.
+ * The Sensor Manager's PROX_LIGHT sensor reports the illuminance in the
+ * first value of its ambient light samples as whole lux (checked on the
+ * Samsung SM-T825's Capella CM3323: 64 in a room, 0 under a thumb; the
+ * second value is a raw count). This driver covers sensor cores with an
+ * ambient light data type; a proximity data type is not handled yet.
  */
 
 #include <linux/mod_devicetable.h>
@@ -37,10 +38,9 @@
 		*val = priv->sensor->data_types[0].cur_sample_rate;
 		return IIO_VAL_INT;
 	case IIO_CHAN_INFO_SCALE:
-		/* Q16 lux */
+		/* whole lux */
 		*val = 1;
-		*val2 = 16;
-		return IIO_VAL_FRACTIONAL_LOG2;
+		return IIO_VAL_INT;
 	}
 
 	return -EINVAL;
